      ":question/id": "1a5df81e-c438-5678-ad1d-5b5e69762c73",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x) = x^{-2}\\log_{4} x$, find $f^{′}(x)$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)=x^{-2}$ and $v(x)=\\log_{4} x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =(x^{-2})^{′}\\log_{4} x+x^{-2}(\\log_{4} x)^{′} \\\\  & =(- \\frac{2}{x^{3}})(\\log_{4} x)+(x^{-2})(\\frac{1}{x \\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}}) \\\\  & =x^{-3}(-2\\log_{4} x + \\frac{1}{\\ln 4})\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "393a4509-2a25-5590-a57d-05d674f87c6d",
