    "question": {
      ":question/id": "1d59fa00-4eae-5577-b605-35141823f62b",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x)=\\tan(x)\\log(x),$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n**Hint:** $\\log(x)=\\log_{10}(x)$\n\n$f^{\\prime}(x)=$\n{{field-1}} $+\\,\\frac{\\tan{\\left(x \\right)}}{x \\ln{\\left(10 \\right)}}$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)=\\tan(x)$ and $v(x)=\\log(x).$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =(\\tan(x))^{′}\\log(x)+\\tan(x)(\\log(x))^{′} \\\\  & =(\\sec^{2}(x))(\\log(x))+(\\tan(x))(\\frac{1}{x\\ln(10)}) \\\\  & =\\sec^{2}(x)\\log(x)+\\frac{\\tan(x)}{x\\ln(10)}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "b082ab67-5673-5417-99f8-881a3864bb7f",
          ":answer-field/key": "field-1",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/blank",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "68fc12a0-40b3-5373-9bc9-0a3d163c5409",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\ln{\\left(x \\right)} \\sec^{2}{\\left(x \\right)}}{\\ln{\\left(10 \\right)}}"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "68fc12a0-40b3-5373-9bc9-0a3d163c5409"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
