    "question": {
      ":question/id": "4d55bcf7-5385-5e74-93cb-6a42a19c3716",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x)={2}^{x}\\log _{7} (x),$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n$f^{\\prime}(x)=$\n{{field-1}} $+\\,\\frac{2^{x}}{x \\ln{\\left(7 \\right)}}$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)={2}^{x}$ and $v(x)=\\log _{7} (x).$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & ={({2}^{x})}^{′}\\log _{7} (x)+{2}^{x}{(\\log _{7} (x))}^{′} \\\\  & =({2}^{x}\\ln  (2))(\\log _{7} (x))+({2}^{x})(\\frac{1}{x\\ln  (7)}) \\\\  & ={2}^{x}\\ln  (2)\\log _{7} (x)+\\frac{{2}^{x}}{x\\ln  (7)}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "0e8f77ed-231e-5425-9e25-f74ab7b6c101",
          ":answer-field/key": "field-1",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/blank",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "1867b6a3-a150-5bc2-91dc-b8b8c6449844",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{2^{x} \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}}{\\ln{\\left(7 \\right)}}"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "1867b6a3-a150-5bc2-91dc-b8b8c6449844"
          ]
        }
